WEBVTT

00:00:00.241 --> 00:00:03.232
Here's the graph of three minus t, shaded

00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:05.179
from zero up to x equals two.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:06.835
Let's give it a meaning.

00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:10.051
A shopping centre car park opens at nine.

00:00:10.995 --> 00:00:13.722
For t hours after that, cars arrive faster

00:00:13.743 --> 00:00:15.888
than they leave, at a net rate of

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.355
three minus t hundred cars an hour.

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:21.686
After noon that rate is negative, so more

00:00:21.727 --> 00:00:23.029
cars leave than arrive.

00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:26.940
The shaded signed area is A of x,

00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:29.627
the integral from zero to x of three

00:00:29.709 --> 00:00:30.991
minus t, d t.

00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:34.429
It counts the extra cars, in hundreds, since

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:34.751
nine.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.040
We use t inside the integral, so that

00:00:38.282 --> 00:00:39.804
x is free to be the moving end.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.494
Think for a moment.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.851
When does A grow fastest, and when is

00:00:44.872 --> 00:00:46.037
the car park fullest?

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:52.491
Let's track A with shapes, like last video.

00:00:53.415 --> 00:00:55.983
Up to one, the region is a trapezium

00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:58.711
with heights three and two, so A of

00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:00.016
one is two and a half.

00:01:00.797 --> 00:01:02.781
Up to two, it's a trapezium with heights

00:01:02.942 --> 00:01:05.407
three and one, so A of two is

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:05.768
four.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.635
Up to three, it's a triangle, so A

00:01:08.696 --> 00:01:10.160
of three is four and a half.

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:13.368
Past three, the graph is below the axis,

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.233
so new strips subtract.

00:01:15.876 --> 00:01:17.906
A of four is four, and A of

00:01:18.028 --> 00:01:19.354
six is back to zero.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.269
Plot these points, and A of x makes

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.078
a smooth curve, like a hill.

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:26.721
Now compare the hill with the height of

00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:27.566
the graph below it.

00:01:28.371 --> 00:01:30.479
At the start, the height is three, the

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.109
biggest it gets, and A climbs fastest.

00:01:33.974 --> 00:01:36.185
At three, the height is zero, and A

00:01:36.206 --> 00:01:37.713
is flat, at the top of the hill.

00:01:38.356 --> 00:01:40.160
That's noon, and the car park is at

00:01:40.201 --> 00:01:42.686
its fullest, because cars have stopped piling up.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:46.036
After that, the height is negative, and A

00:01:46.118 --> 00:01:46.417
falls.

00:01:47.321 --> 00:01:50.006
At x equals one, A has gradient two,

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:52.011
and the height there is two.

00:01:52.874 --> 00:01:55.420
It looks like the gradient of A equals

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.344
the height of the graph, at every x.

00:01:58.324 --> 00:01:58.811
Here's why.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.262
Call the graph

00:02:00.843 --> 00:02:00.924
f,

00:02:01.585 --> 00:02:04.112
so f of t is three minus t.

00:02:05.014 --> 00:02:07.098
Move the end from x to a little

00:02:07.179 --> 00:02:08.723
further, x plus h.

00:02:09.545 --> 00:02:12.534
A gains one thin strip, with width h.

00:02:13.256 --> 00:02:15.481
Its height is about f of x, so

00:02:15.681 --> 00:02:17.986
A grows by about f of x times

00:02:18.307 --> 00:02:18.347
h.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:19.771
Divide by h,

00:02:20.354 --> 00:02:22.743
and the gradient of the chord on A

00:02:23.145 --> 00:02:24.369
is about f of x.

00:02:25.073 --> 00:02:26.980
That's the gradient from first principles.

00:02:27.924 --> 00:02:30.232
At x equals one, with h equal to

00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:32.921
a half, the chord's gradient is one point

00:02:32.982 --> 00:02:33.624
seven five.

00:02:34.347 --> 00:02:36.417
With h equal to a tenth, it's one

00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:37.463
point nine five.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:38.386
As h

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.994
shrinks, the strip's top gets flatter, because the

00:02:42.016 --> 00:02:43.097
curve is continuous.

00:02:43.559 --> 00:02:46.076
So the gradient becomes exactly f of x.

00:02:46.795 --> 00:02:50.464
So differentiating the accumulated area gives back the

00:02:50.505 --> 00:02:50.725
height.

00:02:51.508 --> 00:02:53.792
In words, the area grows at a rate

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.997
equal to the height at its moving edge.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.884
If f is a rate, the amount built

00:02:58.985 --> 00:03:00.929
up so far grows at that rate.

00:03:01.632 --> 00:03:03.175
For the car park, the count of extra

00:03:03.236 --> 00:03:05.601
cars grows at the net rate cars come

00:03:05.662 --> 00:03:05.721
in.

00:03:06.666 --> 00:03:07.069
Check it here.

00:03:07.775 --> 00:03:10.464
The trapezium from zero to x has heights

00:03:10.686 --> 00:03:13.656
three and three minus x, and width x.

00:03:14.199 --> 00:03:15.120
So A of x

00:03:15.622 --> 00:03:18.188
is three x, minus a half x squared.

00:03:18.971 --> 00:03:21.618
Its derivative is three minus x, the graph

00:03:21.639 --> 00:03:22.240
we started with.

00:03:22.843 --> 00:03:25.251
So A is a primitive of f.

00:03:26.041 --> 00:03:28.070
Is this only a trick for straight lines?

00:03:28.795 --> 00:03:29.419
Try a curve.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:33.159
Shade under t squared, from zero up to

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:33.219
x.

00:03:34.404 --> 00:03:36.725
This time we can't use simple shapes, so

00:03:36.745 --> 00:03:39.407
a graphing application adds up very thin strips

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.727
for us, and plots A of x as

00:03:41.949 --> 00:03:42.409
x moves.

00:03:43.132 --> 00:03:45.365
Watch the gradient of A as a point

00:03:45.407 --> 00:03:45.909
moves along.

00:03:46.614 --> 00:03:49.346
It traces x squared, as closely as the

00:03:49.387 --> 00:03:49.949
strips allow.

00:03:50.653 --> 00:03:52.359
Try it in a graphing app: move x

00:03:52.541 --> 00:03:52.901
and watch.

00:03:53.745 --> 00:03:55.749
And a primitive of x squared is x

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.676
cubed over three, which matches the plotted curve.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:02.047
The edge-strip reason didn't need a straight line.

00:04:02.551 --> 00:04:04.317
It only needed a continuous curve.

00:04:05.028 --> 00:04:07.196
What if we start counting at ten o'clock,

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.567
t equals one, instead of nine?

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.771
Every value of A loses the same piece,

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.472
the trapezium from zero to one, which is

00:04:15.573 --> 00:04:17.093
two and a half, the two hundred and

00:04:17.134 --> 00:04:19.115
fifty cars that came in before ten.

00:04:19.856 --> 00:04:22.687
So the whole curve slides down by two

00:04:22.708 --> 00:04:24.755
and a half, and none of its gradients

00:04:24.836 --> 00:04:25.217
change.

00:04:26.001 --> 00:04:28.212
At x equals two, the gradient is still

00:04:28.514 --> 00:04:29.498
one, the height there.

00:04:30.183 --> 00:04:32.227
A different start gives a different primitive,

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.233
one that differs by a constant.

00:04:34.796 --> 00:04:36.584
That's the plus C from primitives.

00:04:37.351 --> 00:04:38.061
Now the big result.

00:04:38.649 --> 00:04:40.078
Take any primitive F of f.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.239
Any two primitives differ by a constant, so

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.528
F of x equals A of x, plus

00:04:46.609 --> 00:04:46.749
C.

00:04:47.693 --> 00:04:48.173
At the start,

00:04:48.675 --> 00:04:51.240
A of a is zero, because no strips

00:04:51.261 --> 00:04:51.942
have been added yet.

00:04:52.624 --> 00:04:54.988
So F of b, minus F of a,

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.875
is A of b plus C, minus C.

00:04:58.577 --> 00:05:00.927
The constants cancel, and that leaves A of

00:05:01.008 --> 00:05:01.208
b,

00:05:01.731 --> 00:05:02.775
the integral from a to b.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:06.156
That's the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus.

00:05:07.001 --> 00:05:09.366
For a continuous f, the integral from a

00:05:09.728 --> 00:05:11.492
to b of f of x, d x,

00:05:11.914 --> 00:05:14.499
equals F of b minus F of a,

00:05:14.861 --> 00:05:16.063
for any primitive F.

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:18.254
We write it with square brackets:

00:05:18.838 --> 00:05:20.224
F of x, from a to b.

00:05:20.822 --> 00:05:22.416
Now check the earlier results.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.771
The trolley's strips settled near two point six

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:26.373
six seven.

00:05:26.975 --> 00:05:29.662
A primitive of x squared is x cubed

00:05:29.822 --> 00:05:30.444
over three,

00:05:30.945 --> 00:05:33.091
so the integral from zero to two is

00:05:33.271 --> 00:05:34.896
eight thirds, minus zero.

00:05:35.437 --> 00:05:37.166
That's about two point six six seven.

00:05:38.072 --> 00:05:39.623
The rain gauge's strips settled on one.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:43.034
A primitive of cos x is sine x,

00:05:43.796 --> 00:05:46.280
and sine of pi over two, minus sine

00:05:46.321 --> 00:05:48.003
of zero, is exactly one.

00:05:48.724 --> 00:05:51.451
And the bath's thirty-two litres come from twelve

00:05:51.491 --> 00:05:53.015
t minus t squared.

00:05:53.777 --> 00:05:56.365
Ninety-six minus sixty-four is thirty-two.

00:05:57.128 --> 00:05:59.534
So instead of adding thousands of strips, we

00:05:59.554 --> 00:06:01.619
need two values of one primitive.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:03.441
Here's the pair to remember.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.514
Differentiate the area, and you get the height.

00:06:07.236 --> 00:06:09.319
Integrate the rate, and you get the change.

00:06:10.021 --> 00:06:11.745
The first is why the second works.

00:06:14.437 --> 00:06:14.881
Your turn.

00:06:15.606 --> 00:06:17.410
A of x is the integral from two

00:06:17.432 --> 00:06:19.296
to x, of the square root of one

00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:20.860
plus t cubed, d t.

00:06:21.704 --> 00:06:22.607
Find A of two,

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.314
and A prime of two.

00:06:24.978 --> 00:06:25.780
Pause here to answer.

00:06:39.975 --> 00:06:42.727
A of two is zero, because from two

00:06:42.788 --> 00:06:44.435
to two there's no strip at all.

00:06:45.279 --> 00:06:47.622
For the gradient, the area grows at the

00:06:47.724 --> 00:06:48.724
height of its edge,

00:06:49.307 --> 00:06:51.390
so A prime of x is the square

00:06:51.431 --> 00:06:53.153
root of one plus x cubed.

00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:56.041
At two, that's the square root of nine,

00:06:56.223 --> 00:06:57.205
which is three.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.648
A prime of two equals two is wrong.

00:07:01.172 --> 00:07:03.888
It differentiates the square root, instead of reading

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:04.311
the height.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:06.413
Last one.

00:07:07.239 --> 00:07:10.628
Use the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus to evaluate

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.377
the integral from one to three, of three

00:07:13.639 --> 00:07:14.901
x squared, d x.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.601
Pause here to answer.

00:07:27.396 --> 00:07:29.852
A primitive of three x squared is x

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:30.295
cubed.

00:07:30.718 --> 00:07:33.440
So the integral is three cubed, minus one

00:07:33.481 --> 00:07:36.724
cubed, which is twenty-seven minus one, or twenty-six.

00:07:37.449 --> 00:07:38.254
Any primitive works.

00:07:38.698 --> 00:07:40.526
Add five to it, and the fives cancel.

00:07:41.271 --> 00:07:42.298
Twenty-seven is wrong.

00:07:42.802 --> 00:07:44.391
It forgets to subtract F of one.

00:07:46.041 --> 00:07:48.145
So the area grows at the height of

00:07:48.205 --> 00:07:48.646
its edge,

00:07:49.147 --> 00:07:51.392
and that turns a definite integral into a

00:07:51.432 --> 00:07:53.557
primitive, evaluated at two ends.

00:07:54.438 --> 00:07:56.360
Next, we'll use it on all kinds of

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.882
integrals, and some of them have negative ends.

00:07:59.647 --> 00:07:59.959
Here's one.

00:08:00.668 --> 00:08:03.585
One third, minus negative two cubed over three.

00:08:04.451 --> 00:08:05.538
Where do the minus signs go?

00:08:08.161 --> 00:08:09.025
Here are the key notes.

00:08:09.427 --> 00:08:10.975
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:11.016 --> 00:08:11.478
to copy them.
